---
system: sys-04-realtime-session-orchestrator
flow_id: ws-handshake
surface: device
spec_anchor: /software/systems/04-realtime-session-orchestrator#connection-handshake
actors: [Device, ALB, Orchestrator, Redis, ControlPlane]
apis:
  - GET /v1/realtime/connect
externals: [Redis]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - invalid_session_token
  - device_inactive
  - concurrent_session_exists
  - service_at_capacity
  - rate_limit_exceeded
idempotency: device_session_id supplied by device — server SETNX device_session:{deviceId} in Redis
retry: device backs off with jitter on 503 E-RT-203
timeout: connect 5s
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED — normalized from _seed.2 (04-realtime#L773).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Device
    participant ALB
    participant Orchestrator
    participant Redis
    participant ControlPlane

    Device->>ALB: GET /v1/realtime/connect?device_id&session_token&protocol_version=1
    ALB->>Orchestrator: WebSocket upgrade
    Orchestrator->>Orchestrator: verify JWT signature, expiry, audience=realtime-orchestrator
    alt invalid_session_token
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 401 E-RT-200
    else device_inactive
        Orchestrator->>ControlPlane: verify device active + ownership
        ControlPlane-->>Orchestrator: 403 device_inactive
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 403 E-RT-201
    else concurrent_session_exists
        Orchestrator->>Redis: GET device_session:{deviceId}
        Redis-->>Orchestrator: existing sessionId
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 409 E-RT-202
    else service_at_capacity
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 503 E-RT-203
    else rate_limit_exceeded
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 429 E-RT-204
    else success
        Orchestrator->>Redis: SET NX device_session:{deviceId} (35min TTL)
        Redis-->>Orchestrator: OK
        Orchestrator-->>Device: 101 Switching Protocols
        Device->>Orchestrator: SESSION_OPEN (0x01)
        Orchestrator-->>Device: SESSION_ACK (0x02) sessionId, maxTurns=60, costCeilingUsd=0.12
    end

    Note over Device,Orchestrator: connect 5s — Redis SETNX enforces single-session invariant — Redis unavailable rejects admission
